   ***************************************************************************
   *************************** Hamiltonian defined ***************************
   ***************************************************************************

 * Print level:    0
 * Dirac-Coulomb Hamiltonian
 * Kohn-Sham calculation using the xc functional: LDA
 * SS integrals neglected:
   Interatomic Coulombic SS-contributions modelled by
   classical repulsion of small component atomic charges
   using tabulated charges.
 * Default integral flags passed to all modules
   - LL-integrals:     1
   - LS-integrals:     1
   - SS-integrals:     0
   - GT-integrals:     0
 * Basis set:
   - contracted large component basis set
   - uncontracted small component basis set


 Information about the restricted kinetic balance scheme:
 * Default RKB projection:
   1: Pre-projection in scalar basis
   2: Removal of unphysical solutions (via diagonalization of free particle Hamiltonian)
 File with embedding potentia (=fdepot) is h2o_in_2h2o.vemb                                            
 File with frozen density (+gradient etc) (=fdedns) is h2o_in_2h2o.frzdens                                         
  
 =====================================================================================================
 Frozen Density Embedding to include enviroment effects using the fixed potential method described in:
 A.S.P. Gomes, C. R. Jacob and L. Visscher, Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 10 (2008) 5353–5362.
 =====================================================================================================

  Frozen Density Embedding Calculation set-up:
  --------------------------------------------

 * Print level:     0
 * FDE Potential read from file: h2o_in_2h2o.vemb                                            
 * Density (and gradient) from frozen subsystems read from file: h2o_in_2h2o.frzdens                                         


   Kohn-Sham calculation set-up
   ----------------------------

 * Print level:     2
 * Numerical integration grid:
   - radial quadrature according to R. Lindh, P.-Aa. Malmqvist, and L. Gagliardi
     precision of radial quadrature set to:  0.10000E-12
   - angular quadrature using the Lebedev scheme, exact up to order L = 41
